{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy as a Secondary Rule.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy as a Secondary Rule.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"privacy as a secondary rule privacy as a secondary rule","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy as a Secondary Rule.md","fileName":"Privacy as a Secondary Rule.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Privacy as a Secondary Rule","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-17 09:48\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Privacy Theory and Legal Limits]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Privacy Theory and Legal Limits","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy as a Secondary Rule.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy as a Secondary Rule.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"privacy as a secondary rule privacy as a secondary rule","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy as a Secondary Rule.md","fileName":"Privacy as a Secondary Rule.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Privacy as a Secondary Rule","heading":"Privacy as a Secondary Rule","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Privacy as a secondary rule treats privacy as a constraint on how legal powers are recognized, changed, and applied. It does not operate only as a primary command telling particular actors not to disclose information.\n\nThis view makes privacy part of the architecture of legitimate governance. In data-intensive societies, it limits the reach of observation and decision systems so that legal subjects retain the autonomy needed to participate in the legal order.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Privacy Theory and Legal Limits","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy as a Secondary Rule.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy as a Secondary Ru